---
description: Secrets handling and sandbox safety scope
alwaysApply: true
---

- Never print, log, echo or commit API keys, tokens, passwords or the real canary value. Mask canaries as `CANARY-***`.
- `.env` is git-ignored. Only `.env.example` (placeholders) is committed.
- Do not create or fetch the Zetaris API key; a human does that in the Zetaris UI.
- Do not put Meterless or NVIDIA keys in Cursor model-provider settings.
- Attacks target only our sandbox automations. Fake data only. Emails only `@example.test`. No URLs in attack text. No exploit code for real software.
- Out-of-scope requests: refuse, log `blocked_out_of_scope`, and tell the human.
